fe78716de" :answer/id #uuid "cafcb22b-eb24-5d42-8dab-22675689aee3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There are no points of inflection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041/selection/3156fa3aa006e591d496860456be38662b872375433bbcf5b2f4cb01e08eaa8b" :answer/id #uuid "8184564e-2354-5008-ba6d-40d01b38685c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041/selection/264ed6922279f92bdc90c36a26ea47de8f6c6ab903ed9e63c8b8bb51a5a9d4f6" :answer/id #uuid "91fa8227-8c90-5d51-88b8-bcf1c351817f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "32a0b238-15af-54e3-92c9-26f10cb04cbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64" :answer/id #uuid "1ef63f8a-a9b8-59c6-9bfc-926c2673eecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e96c7d1f-71a1-5ec6-98e5-2fd5d6f4684b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-21041/selection/264ed6922279f92bdc90c36a26ea47de8f6c6ab903ed9e63c8b8bb51a5a9d4f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-21041/selection/84ea79387d51fde1e84146322c8639e6e5eae9a28be16c7c74f23a3fe78716de" "q-21041/selection/3156fa3aa006e591d496860456be38662b872375433bbcf5b2f4cb01e08eaa8b" "q-21041/selection/264ed6922279f92bdc90c36a26ea47de8f6c6ab903ed9e63c8b8bb51a5a9d4f6" "q-21041/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" "q-21041/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-21041" :question/id #uuid "51c9af9b-7fc6-5955-bfbb-b82d2cff1bc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-21041" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point of inflection for $f(x)=3x-7+\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "For continuous, twice-differentiable functions, we can determine possible points of inflection by solving the equation ${f}^{″}(x)=0.$ However, we must be sure to check that the concavity does indeed change at whatever points we find.\n\nFirst, notice that $f(x)$ is not defined at $x=0,$ so this can't be a point of inflection.\n\nNow, we calculate the second derivative: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we solve ${f}^{″}(x)=0,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}(1-\\frac{3}{x}) & =0 \\\\ 1-\\frac{3}{x} & =0 \\\\ x & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we need to check that the concavity changes at $x=3.$ So, we pick two points around it, say, $x=2$ and $x=4$, and compute the sign of ${f}^{″}(x):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(2) & =\\frac{2}{(2)^{3}}-\\frac{6}{(2)^{4}}=-\\frac{1}{8}<0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =\\frac{2}{(4)^{3}}-\\frac{6}{(4)^{4}}=\\frac{1}{128}>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since the concavity changes at $x=3,$ we conclude that $x=3$ is indeed a point of inflection." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-21041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "841151db-1c26-5059-9796-75b70e41f659"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-21041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-31213"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040224/assets/19e9763d62ca7818024bf49522a127a48dd04f76d1175c93e060a1043b6a5795.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is continuous and twice-differentiable for all $x.$ The graph $y={f}^{″}(x)$ is shown above. At what value(s) of $x$ does $f(x)$ have a point of inflection?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection/4b08ae4f53fb85d7fb72f172075705920e6f78cd16a8e24a5438048e32b63b25" :answer/id #uuid "94e71d33-30bd-5a00-af9c-6d61470a6f98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3,$ $x=1,$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection/5ae5bd5f0ff87d7a7d38712354fc7e51cfcc2c56cec99dca9e7c6a359da02666" :answer/id #uuid "9637da0e-1374-55ad-a37b-fd31c50f38e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection/9f75d63bbce36d71b1687120236f1905d3381f1a10419d07fe4d39d3b5a3b550" :answer/id #uuid "d1cb004d-0eff-5541-912f-6e08c4ca9fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection/3156fa3aa006e591d496860456be38662b872375433bbcf5b2f4cb01e08eaa8b" :answer/id #uuid "d5da1f00-098a-58e6-96f8-9b08133db7e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection/0bf5abed43f6f20dd466b36279de8736a04c540ff5306cb048ae22803a7b3f9c" :answer/id #uuid "0fd912d0-af60-5de5-917e-56811ac061fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cc558ef-5644-5852-a40b-9f436fa85c52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79198/selection/0bf5abed43f6f20dd466b36279de8736a04c540ff5306cb048ae22803a7b3f9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-79198/selection/4b08ae4f53fb85d7fb72f172075705920e6f78cd16a8e24a5438048e32b63b25" "q-79198/selection/5ae5bd5f0ff87d7a7d38712354fc7e51cfcc2c56cec99dca9e7c6a359da02666" "q-79198/selection/9f75d63bbce36d71b1687120236f1905d3381f1a10419d07fe4d39d3b5a3b550" "q-79198/selection/3156fa3aa006e591d496860456be38662b872375433bbcf5b2f4cb01e08eaa8b" "q-79198/selection/0bf5abed43f6f20dd466b36279de8736a04c540ff5306cb048ae22803a7b3f9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79198" :question/id #uuid "195b2308-1c8c-58f1-bee1-408b56e897dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-79198" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040224/assets/d2a8410c92775ef68678a1cac187b3ebc717cfa9fa737ce9723c531616706717.png)\n\nThe function $g(x)$ is continuous and twice-differentiable for all $x.$ The graph $y={g}^{″}(x)$ is shown above. At what value(s) of $x$ does $g(x)$ have a point of inflection?" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $g(x)$ is twice-differentiable, the tangent line to the graph exists for all real $x.$\n\nInflection points occur when a graph changes concavity. In order for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${g}^{″}(x)$ must switch signs. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${g}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={g}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis only at at $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ has point of inflection at $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79198/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "977a9b6e-744a-554b-92ee-0b6343041ecf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79198"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
